  "body": "## Stage 5: encrypted Playwright session storage\n\nPlaywright storage-state files contain authenticated marketplace cookies/localStorage and were previously persisted as plaintext `sessions/bot-<id>.json` files. This PR makes persistent session material encrypted and upgrade-safe without changing offer/negotiation behavior.\n\n### Security and runtime behavior\n- stores persistent session state as AES-256-GCM `bot-<id>.state.enc`\n- binds ciphertext to the owning bot ID with AES-GCM AAD so session files cannot be swapped between bots\n- never writes plaintext Playwright storage state to a temporary disk file; decrypted JSON is passed to Playwright via `setStorageState(String)` in memory\n- supports dedicated `FLIPBOT_SESSION_ENCRYPTION_KEY`, falling back to `FLIPBOT_ENCRYPTION_KEY`\n- uses owner-only POSIX permissions where supported (`0700` directory, `0600` files)\n- legacy plaintext `.json` migrates only after encrypted state is written, read back and authenticated\n- an existing encrypted file is never overwritten unless the currently configured key first authenticates it\n- if encrypted state cannot be opened because the worker has a missing/wrong key, the file is left untouched and the browser job starts clean so normal login can continue\n- if legacy plaintext cannot yet migrate, it can still be restored in memory for that run instead of breaking the upgrade\n- removes session files only for bot IDs that no longer exist; STOPPED bots keep their session\n\n### Tests\n- ciphertext-only at rest + round trip\n- owner-only permissions where supported\n- legacy plaintext migration\n- wrong-key read fails closed\n- wrong key cannot overwrite prior valid ciphertext\n- ciphertext is bound to bot ID\n- orphan cleanup preserves existing bots\n- legacy upgrade fallback remains usable\n- corrupted/unavailable encrypted state falls back to clean context without deleting the file\n- Bot API all-bots parsing used by cleanup\n\nNo database schema or real-action logic is changed.",
